    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Banking refers to the activity of accepting deposits from the public and providing loans and advances. Banks act as financial intermediaries between savers and borrowers.",
      "id": "vkszjjw"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Banking system in India is regulated by the Reserve Bank of India (RBI) under the Banking Regulation Act, 1949.",
      "id": "cfxndrf"
    },
    {
