      "id": "rkzzduw",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "5. CREDIT CREATION"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Banks create credit by lending out a portion of deposits while keeping required reserves.",
      "id": "d8147yo"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Credit Multiplier = 1 / CRR",
      "id": "zkqs6hi"
    },
    {
      "id": "adg7o05",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "6. NATIONALISATION OF BANKS"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "In 1969, 14 major banks were nationalised.<br/>In 1980, 6 more banks were nationalised.",
      "id": "x2rgg0v"
    },
    {
      "type": "pullQuote",
      "content": "Banks act as financial intermediaries between savers and borrowers.",
      "id": "utaxczd"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Objective was to expand banking in rural areas and support priority sectors.",
      "id": "6i2hge4"
    },
    {
      "id": "5wdrfhq",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "7. NON-PERFORMING ASSETS (NPA)"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "A loan becomes NPA when interest or principal remains overdue for more than 90 days.",
      "id": "bjgxddo"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "High NPAs affect bank profitability and capital adequacy.",
      "id": "7oe79ve"
    },
    {
      "id": "l4gpdqf",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "8. FINANCIAL INCLUSION"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Financial inclusion aims to provide affordable banking services to all citizens.",
      "id": "b6sf5lt"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Major initiatives include Jan Dhan Yojana, Direct Benefit Transfer (DBT), and digital payments.",
      "id": "385u5qp"
    },
    {
      "id": "aprli3e",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "9.PRIORITY SECTOR LENDING (PSL)"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Priority Sector Lending (PSL) is an RBI policy that mandates banks to lend a specified portion of their total credit to key sectors of the economy.",
      "id": "ksflka2"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Target: 40% of Adjusted Net Bank Credit (ANBC) for domestic commercial banks.",
      "id": "r1z03vg"
    },
