    {
      "id": "l9707zv",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "10. CAPITAL ADEQUACY RATIO (CAR)"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "CAR measures a bank’s capital relative to its risk-weighted assets.",
      "id": "2v7rxh1"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Formula: CAR = (Tier 1 Capital + Tier 2 Capital) / Risk Weighted Assets × 100",
      "id": "coftrdr"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Minimum requirement in India: 9% (as per RBI, Basel III norms).",
      "id": "wnny8eg"
    },
    {
      "id": "95rn0r2",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "11. BASEL NORMS LINKAGE"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Basel norms are international banking regulations issued by the Basel Committee on Banking Supervision.",
      "id": "bc8mxij"
    },
